Subject: [PATCH 7/7] relax live: an edit saved right after `inspect pin on`
 waits for the unpin

The watch loop looks at PINNED at the top of a round and then sleeps on the
file events. A pin set during that sleep was not seen: the next save woke the
round and it applied the edit, so the first edit after every `pin on` reached
the pinned app (2 of 2 here). The round looks again after the wait and leaves
the save to the unpin's whole scan.

Checked on a running program: 3 of 3 edits held while pinned and applied on
unpin; a two-step edit (a call first, the fn it calls second) made while pinned
never reached the app half done and landed as one patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/relax/compiler/src/reload.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/relax/compiler/src/reload.rs b/libs/relax/compiler/src/reload.rs
index 3d790e0e..842f8eea 100644
--- a/libs/relax/compiler/src/reload.rs
+++ b/libs/relax/compiler/src/reload.rs
@@ -9321,6 +9321,9 @@ unsafe fn watch(up: *mut Unit, mut inputs: Inputs) {
             _ => std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(5)),
         }
         let woke = Instant::now();
+        // pinned while the watch waited (`inspect pin on` came after the check above): the save
+        // that woke it is not applied, the unpin's whole scan finds it
+        if PINNED.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Acquire) { continue; }
         if DOMAIN_LOADING.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Acquire) { gate_note(1); continue; }
         let latest = DOMAIN_REVISION.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Acquire);
         if latest != revision {
